With `--depth 1`, a directory given as `input` and as `./input/` prints each directory summary once, counting each file once: `input/sub/` holds two files, not four. Directory summaries use the same normal form as file summaries.
== args
--depth
1
input
./input/
== file input/top.md
# Top
== file input/sub/one.md
# One
== file input/sub/two.md
# Two
== stdout
glob view: input ./input/
input/sub/ (2 files, 2 lines)
input/top.md (1 line): # Top
== stderr
== exit 0
